JFtn follow-up work
===================

Reviewed against the source and tests on 2026-10-20.
Implemented behavior and limits are documented under docs/.

Remaining implementation
------------------------

- Move FileEcho DAO queries/mappings behind a typed backend adapter while preserving
  existing area/access/creation tables and SQL-free file mode. It already shares
  the main mail source; see docs/storage.md for the remaining portability boundary.

- Add full archive/body search and optional trash for browser mail readers.
  Local filtering of loaded message headers/excerpts is already available.
- Refine the mobile mail layout after desktop review; retain separate list,
  reader and composer screens, readable controls and dirty-draft protection.
- Add safe link removal/renaming, accounting for routes, subscriptions and queues.
  Netmail routing policy/rule administration and preview now exist in RPC/UI.
- Decide whether to implement or remove the empty legacy JAMEchoBase.getMessage()
  and delMessage() methods. JamArea and the JAM bridge already support mail access.
- Add durable automatic poll retries/backoff and incoming-session tracking.
  Outgoing queue inspection, manual polling/retry, cancellation, history and
  per-attempt journals already work through RPC/UI.
- Define explicit administration of prepared outbound deliveries (for example,
  hold/release/removal), including safety while a transport owns a file.
  Outbound inspection and existing routing/Hold behavior are already implemented.
- Add safe retention/cleanup for mail delivery receipts, processing/script/JAM
  journals and received-file archives. Poll history already has count-based
  retention via PollHistoryLimit, and pruning also deletes its attempt journals.
- Expand fault-injection tests for sender deadlines, disk-full/close/fsync failures
  and crash boundaries across supported platforms. Restart/recovery, malformed
  input, connection failure and cross-process JAM locking already have tests.
- Extend real BSO/HTick coverage to interrupted large transfers and additional
  request processors. Real binkd FLO/REQ consumption, SRIF responses, post-ACK
  KFS/TFS, hold/busy recovery and two-way HTick toss/hatch/Replaces now have
  container tests. Runbook and fixture boundaries: docs/husky-integration.md.
- Add explicit stopped-node storage/profile migration tooling. Full/Headless,
  JAM/MSG Legacy and SQL-free Transit now have separate installation profiles.
  Current recovery/switching constraints: docs/transit-profiles.md.

Optional future scope (not committed features)
---------------------------------------------

- Investigate checksum interoperability with New Point Keeper R46 pointlists.
  An observed PNT46REG.289 publication declares CRC 45257 while canonical CRLF
  CRC-16/XMODEM computes 40818 (raw LF also differs). Node lists and generated
  point fixtures pass. Real unmodified historical Husky nlcrc also rejects all
  75 received publications; a public 2024 New Point Keeper sample fails too.
  Strict import remains the default. Explicit DirectoryIgnoreCRC source/filename
  rules now allow full-list recovery without disabling structural/TIC validation.
  Compare the exact upstream original/generator to explain the wrong CRCs.

- Select additional binkp/TIC extensions or services only with explicit protocol
  requirements and interoperability/security tests; current limits are in docs/.
- Add additional SQL provider implementations and test each repository contract
  against the actual backend. Typed storage SPI and the H2 adapters now exist;
  physical database/profile migration remains an explicit separate operation.
- Consider an RSS posting robot.
- Consider further Husky robot commands and a dedicated uplink-request UI only
  with matching backend support: upstream %AVAIL catalogs, date-based/unlimited
  rescan, compression/size policy, rules delivery and remote credential changes.
  Current command support, safe limits and CLI/script requests: docs/mail-robots.md.

Current scope and test limits:
- docs/ui-rpc-plugin-plan.md (completed implementation record)
- docs/mail-robots.md
- docs/tosser.md
- docs/rpc-ui.md
- docs/web-ui.md
- docs/test-coverage.md
